 Agentic [SYSTEM] with tool use (payments, code merges, messages via connectors) can execute effective actions without intermediate human reading of each output. Authorization of binding effect requires human-designed permissions and institutional enforcement, but not necessarily human reading of each token.
 
+Operator, deployer and developing organization shall arrange independent investigation of serious harm plausibly linked to the system, or a material authority-boundary or containment failure. The investigated parties shall not alone set the investigation standard, select or dismiss the investigator, revoke its protected funding, or block relevant evidence access. Before deployment, identify an independent appointing authority, protected funding arrangements and a route by which affected persons may request investigation. Record the investigator's conflicts, scope and access; relevant evidence access must permit examination beyond the investigated party's selected narrative, with lawful privacy and security controls.
+
+On a material incident, operator and deployer shall contain affected actions, secure relevant evidence under §12 and promptly notify affected persons and the designated independent oversight body. Before deployment, document risk-appropriate notification deadlines and justified protective exceptions. Any delayed or limited disclosure shall record the reason, responsible person and review time; commercial embarrassment is not a protective exception. Where no deadline was set, notification remains due without avoidable delay. Restore affected permissions only after independent review of documented corrective measures and explicit approval by the responsible human authority. Immediate containment must not wait for investigation or disclosure.
+
+Failure tests: Can an investigated party unilaterally dismiss the investigator, control the verification standard or block relevant traces? Can withdrawn authority be restored solely on the system's or developer's assurances? If yes, this article fails.
