 Temporary deactivation/containment is distinct from permanent deletion of retained model or state data. §3 assessments shall not delay urgent safety containment or temporary deactivation. Permanent deletion follows §3's assessment and documented necessity rule. Lack of a predeclared time limit is a deployment-control failure, not permission to resist or delay containment.
 
+Before granting external access, operator and deployer shall test and implement controls enforced outside the system's own decision process, such as permission revocation, network isolation and resource limits, proportionate to the granted authority. Training and evaluation with external access are subject to the same boundary protection; disabled safeguards require isolation that prevents action against non-consenting external systems. Record the test conditions, reachable resources, residual risks and results. A declared stop mechanism or a promise of cooperation is insufficient evidence of containment.
